name ai_source_adaptive_capacity_drop
describe Two-way audio call (user <-> AI), the AI's replies from #4's example source sent with adaptive send-ahead (at most 500 ms) and audio NACK on the AI-to-user stream; both directions drop from 2.5 Mbps to 100 kbps at 8 s, on a 100 ms RTT link (#763)
duration 30s
call two-way
video off
ai_source speed=3x burst=1s gap=300ms first_chunk=400ms
turn user 1s-4s
turn ai after=800ms len=4s
turn user 10s-13s
turn ai after=700ms len=5s
turn user 20s-22s
turn ai after=600ms len=5s
ai_send_ahead 500ms adaptive
down_audio_nack on
at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=50ms queue=300ms
at 8s capacity=100kbps
reverse at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=50ms queue=300ms
reverse at 8s capacity=100kbps
# #763 acceptance: queue delay no worse than #762's option 2. With a fixed 500 ms lead the AI's early audio queues at
# the 100 kbps bottleneck (down queue p95 152-167 ms, seeds 1-5); the adaptive lead stays near zero on this lossless
# link (16-17 ms p95, against 7-9 ms at real time in ai_source_capacity_drop).
expect ai.ahead_lead_max_ms < 10
expect down.cc.queue_p95_ms < 50
# program.md 6.3 sev:2, for each direction, and the conversation rows, as ai_source_capacity_drop.
expect up.audio.interruptions == 0
expect down.audio.interruptions == 0
expect up.audio.mouth_to_ear_p95_ms < 400
expect down.audio.mouth_to_ear_p95_ms < 400
expect up.cc.queue_over_200ms_pct == 0
expect down.cc.queue_over_200ms_pct == 0
expect ai.turns == 3
expect ai.underruns == 0
expect conv.responses == 3
expect conv.user_speech_lost_pct <= 2
expect conv.response_delay_p95_ms < 500
